# Clean URLs for Cloudflare Pages. Canonicals and sitemap.xml use the
# extensionless paths with no trailing slash:
#   /   /about   /services   /find-us
#
# Pages already redirects /about.html and /about/ toward /about. These
# 301s make that permanent. The destination is the URL Pages serves with
# status 200, so the rule does not loop. Do not add the reverse
# (/about → /about.html).
#
# /index.html is special. Pages would send it to /index, which is a
# second copy of the homepage. Send every index form to /.

/index.html   /          301
/index        /          301
/index/       /          301

/about.html   /about     301
/about/       /about     301

/services.html   /services   301
/services/       /services   301

/find-us.html   /find-us   301
/find-us/       /find-us   301

# www.modelbarbers.com → https://modelbarbers.com is not listed here.
# Pages ignores domain-level rules in this file. Create that 301 as a
# Cloudflare Bulk Redirect after DNS is on Cloudflare. See HOSTING.md.
# vercel.json still does this redirect for the current Vercel deploy.
